{"role":"assistant","content":"## Ruling: **(c) withdraw the intra-unit lane from the landing candidate**\n\nKeep the two fixtures honestly `:blocked` at the unchanged **2M** budget. Do not approve 4M.\n\nThe present measurements cannot support an acceptance-budget change:\n\n- They conflict internally: the walker is reported as exhausting at 2M, while option (a) says it completes at 2M.\n- They also conflict with the previously reported D2 counts of walker **1,837,052** and semantic **1,002,469**.\n- D2 is the token-packet design, not the earlier map-record design; the measured implementation and commit identity need to be pinned unambiguously.\n- Completing under a 4M limit does not establish 2× headroom. Actual consumption must be measured; a budget twice the old failing limit is not twice measured usage.\n\nMost importantly, a finite acceptance budget whose exhaustion path can wedge is not a reliable bound. Raising fuel until known fixtures avoid that path would conceal the defect and leave genuine runaways unbounded.\n\n### Separate exhaustion-wedge defect\n\nOpen a **bounded diagnostic-only** investigation, initially without `yin.vm` changes:\n\n1. Pin the exact compiler commit, AST identity, fixture, modules, and instrumentation.\n2. Minimize the D2-generated program that causes semantic budget exhaustion not to return.\n3. Determine whether termination is lost in `run-guest-machine`, observer exception handling, semantic stepping, or the thrown budget-exhaustion path.\n4. Capture the advanced `:consumer`, continuation/control summary, and whether repeated `vm/step` calls advance at all; do not serialize closure environments.\n5. Establish whether walker exhaustion over the same AST terminates normally.\n6. If a shared-runtime change is indicated, return the minimized reproduction for an explicit architectural ruling before editing `yin.vm`.\n\nAny future intra-unit proposal must then provide reproducible per-lane counts on one pinned commit, ordinary termination at exhaustion, and a valid both-evaluator authenticity regression. Fixing the wedge alone would not suffice while the walker still exceeds 2M."}
